    title: "At least 14 killed in weapons depot blast in Syria’s Idlib, state TV says",
    summary: "Authorities have not clarified what caused the explosion near the city of Sarmada.",
    preview: "Authorities have not clarified what caused the explosion near the city of Sarmada. At least 14 people have been killed in an explosion at a temporary depot for weapons and remnants of war near Sarmada, a city in Syria’s Idlib province, according to state television. Wednesday’s blast also injured 11 people, and thick smoke from a resulting fire billowed from the site for hours. Syria’s Defence Ministry said some of its personnel were among those injured, according to the Reuters news agency.",
    body: "Authorities have not clarified what caused the explosion near the city of Sarmada.\n\nAt least 14 people have been killed in an explosion at a temporary depot for weapons and remnants of war near Sarmada, a city in Syria’s Idlib province, according to state television.\n\nWednesday’s blast also injured 11 people, and thick smoke from a resulting fire billowed from the site for hours.\n\nSyria’s Defence Ministry said some of its personnel were among those injured, according to the Reuters news agency.\n\nEarlier, the state news agency reported that emergency teams had been immediately dispatched after the explosion at Burj al-Nimra village in northern Idlib’s countryside.\n\nHowever, secondary explosions hampered firefighting teams from extinguishing the fires.\n\nEmergency teams are searching for survivors trapped under the rubble. An Associated Press news agency photographer reported seeing bodies recovered at the scene.\n\nAuthorities have not clarified what caused the explosion, but incidents like these are common in Syria, which has only recently emerged from more than 10 years of war.\n\nThe destroyed depot was used to store weapons and munitions from the Syrian uprising and civil war, which lasted between 2011 and 2024, according to the Defence Ministry as cited by the SANA state news agency.\n\nEarlier, on September 1, a vehicle carrying ammunition exploded in Binnish, also in Idlib province, killing five people and wounding others, according to Syrian state media.",
